| Mathias Buus | 2 | 0.9% | 2 / 0.8% | 1 |

The other 14 authors hold 4.2% together. The largest of them is Saad Tazi with 0.9%. Damien Klinnert and Typicode each have 0 lines left.

**Bus factor:** 1 for this file. Troy alone holds 67.3% of the non-blank lines (66.8% counting blank lines). It takes 3 authors to reach 80%. Bus factor here means the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines together reach 50%.

## Caveats
- **Troy's two addresses.** I'm counting <email redacted> and troy@laptop.example as one person because the name is the same. The tool rates that as strong evidence, but it's a guess, and nothing is written to `.mailmap`. Counted separately: <email redacted> has 132 lines (61.7%, 28 commits) and troy@laptop.example has 12 lines (1 commit). The commit counts are a separate check: across the whole repo, gmail has 93 commits and laptop has 2.
- **Alejandro's two names.** One address, <email redacted>, also appears as "alex94puchades". The tool already counts both names as one person (14 lines).
- **Reformat `62628c0` (Fiona Formatter) is left out.** It changed only whitespace and quotes across 4 files (1016 lines changed, 428 of them in this file). If it were counted, Fiona would show 32 lines (15.0%) and Troy would drop to 123 (57.5%). Douglas would drop to 16 and Alejandro to 13. That code was written by the earlier authors, not by Fiona.
- **Mechanical rewrites were checked.** Of 31 commits, 1 was set aside (`62628c0`). One more candidate, `fcd2b56` (Troy's ESLint switch), was kept. It made real edits (braces, a split `var`, a removed parameter), and re-running without it gives the same figures.
- Copy detection is the default `-C`. The figures are as of HEAD and attribute all 214 lines.
- These counts say nothing about code quality, review work, or code that was deleted on purpose.

