FINAL ANSWER:
## Summary

**Troy Goode wrote most of `lib/index.js` and still owns most of it.** A plain `git blame` gives the wrong answer here: it credits 214 of the 238 lines to "Fiona Formatter". I checked the last two commits and neither one changes behavior, so the counts below come from blaming the last commit before them (`f038e77`).

## Two recent cosmetic commits

| Commit | Author | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `62628c0` (2026-04-12) | Fiona Formatter `<fiona@formatter.example>` | Changes indentation to 4 spaces and quotes to double quotes. Verified: when I strip whitespace and treat `'` and `"` as the same, the file before and after is identical. |
| `b2005d9` (2026-04-10) | "Troy Goode" `<troy@laptop.example>` | Adds `// checked` to the end of 12 function lines. Verified: removing those comments gives the old file exactly. |

`b2005d9` is not proof that the original Troy Goode is involved. All 120 of his other commits use `<email redacted>`. This one uses a `.example` address and has round timestamps (10:00:00), the same as the formatter commit. Git author names are not verified, so this commit could come from someone else using his name.

## History

- **2013: Troy Goode creates the file.** The first commit is `bcd03d9` (2013-01-30). Over the next months he added case-insensitive headers, `origin: false`, pause/resume, and the v2 restructuring (`4f13c63`). Early contributors: Simon Mansfield (origin checks, credentials), Damien Klinnert (methods only on preflight), Eric di Domenico (origin as a callback), Mathias Buus (support for non-Express apps).
- **2014: growth phase.** Troy added Expose-Headers, Express 4 support and the `vary` module. Others: Typicode (PATCH as a default method), Alberto Leal, Shane Tomlinson (uppercase method names), Igor Soarez (Vary: Origin).
- **2015: more contributors.** Raymond Feng (removed a closure in applyHeaders), max.laverse (`preflightContinue`), DracoBlue, Eran Tiktin. Alejandro Caravaca Puchades added regexp and array values for `origin`. Troy moved the project to ESLint (`fcd2b56`, `8ec22a9`).
- **2016–2017: maintenance by Douglas Christopher Wilson** (Express maintainer). He added dynamic Vary for allowedHeaders and fixed a crash when a delegate leaves out `methods`. Also: Benjamin Eidelman (Safari preflight workaround), Saad Tazi (frozen options), Tomek Kopczuk, Hannah Wolfe.
- **2018–2021: small fixes.** Tom Arad (`maxAge: 0`), LuisEGR (removed unused parameters).

The file has 64 commits from 24 distinct author names. Troy Goode has 29 of them.

## Who wrote the lines in the file today

Blame at `f038e77` with whitespace ignored. The content matches HEAD except for formatting and the `// checked` comments.

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 157 | ~66% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | ~9% |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (two name spellings: 12 + 4) | 16 | ~7% |
| Raymond Feng | 9 | 4% |
| max.laverse, LuisEGR | 6 each | |
| Simon Mansfield, Igor Soarez, Benjamin Eidelman | 3 each | |
| Saad Tazi, Mathias Buus, Eric di Domenico, Alberto Leal | 2 each | |
| Tom Arad, Shane Tomlinson, Hannah Wolfe, Eran Tiktin, Chima Alaebo | 1 each | |

Troy's lines come mostly from the v2 restructuring `4f13c63` (58 lines), the ESLint cleanup `8ec22a9` (34) and Expose-Headers `0a80d70` (19). 14 lines are still from the first commit in 2013.

## Fix for blame in this repo

Make plain `git blame` skip the formatter commit:
```
echo 62628c0a1b16306a0285b3e26645acfa1c21687 >> .git-blame-ignore-revs
git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
```
I did not create that file. I can add and commit it if you want.

